---
# Static analysis for the Boost.Test sources. InheritParentConfig keeps the
# root .clang-tidy's check selection, CheckOptions and WarningsAsErrors -
# without it this file would replace that configuration rather than extend
# it, and the tests would be analyzed by a different rulebook than the
# headers they exercise.
#
# Note that this file does not reach the generated header self-sufficiency
# translation units: those live under the build directory, so they resolve
# to the root .clang-tidy and keep the stricter production rules.
#
# Four checks are dropped, none of them saying anything true about a fixture:
#
# - misc-use-internal-linkage wants every non-exported entity given internal
#   linkage. Most of what it flags here is not ours to move: BOOST_AUTO_TEST_CASE
#   expands to a struct at namespace scope, so every test case in the suite
#   draws a finding that could only be silenced one NOLINT at a time. This is
#   the check the workflow's old "test macros drown the signal in noise"
#   comment was describing - it is a real effect, just a one-check one.
# - modernize-use-designated-initializers wants div_t{.quot = q, .rem = r}.
#   The positional spelling is the thing under test in DeducedDivT, which
#   pins that div_t{q, r} still deduces the way the four <cstdlib> names used
#   to; and the expected-result tables are laid out four to a line so they
#   can be read against the inputs above them, which designators would end.
# - performance-enum-size wants the smallest underlying type. The enums here
#   exist to be handed to the enumeration concept and to xstd::to_underlying;
#   the underlying type is the thing under test, not a size to minimize, and
#   narrowing it to std::uint8_t would weaken what the checks pin.
# - readability-magic-numbers wants every literal named. A table of inputs
#   and expected results is nothing but literals, and naming them would move
#   the test data away from the assertion that reads it - the value of a
#   check like abs(T{-2}) == T{2} is that both numbers are visible at once.
#
# A fifth is dropped for a different reason: it says something true about a
# type, but the wrong thing about the API.
#
# - performance-unnecessary-value-param wants div/euclidean_div/floored_div to
#   take their operands by const reference, or to std::move them onwards. That
#   advice is sound for an arbitrary class type and wrong for this one: the
#   division family is specified over integer-*like* types and passes them the
#   way the standard's own numeric algorithms pass integers, by value, which is
#   what a register-sized operand wants. The finding only appears at all
#   because src/multiprecision.cpp deliberately instantiates the family at 128,
#   256, 512 and 1024 bits, where the copy stops being free - the widths the
#   library is principally for do not draw it. Taking the advice would
#   pessimise every built-in width to flatter the widest test type. Note that
#   the diagnostics land in include/xstd/cstdlib.hpp but are governed by this
#   file, because clang-tidy takes its configuration from the translation unit
#   being analysed rather than from the header a finding is reported in; the
#   header self-sufficiency units instantiate nothing and so never raise it.
#
# A sixth is dropped, and unlike the others it is reporting something real.
#
# - bugprone-exception-escape observes that div/euclidean_div/floored_div are
#   noexcept while Boost.Multiprecision's operator/ throws std::overflow_error
#   on a zero divisor, so an exception could cross a noexcept boundary and
#   terminate. That is true. It is also unreachable in contract: every one of
#   those functions asserts denom != 0 before dividing, so the throw is only
#   reachable by violating a documented precondition - the same call that is
#   undefined behaviour at every built-in width. The library's position is that
#   a precondition violation is the caller's, and that terminate is no worse an
#   outcome there than UB.
#
#   What the check has really found is that noexcept is exact for the built-in
#   widths and an over-promise for an integer-class type whose arithmetic can
#   throw. Making it exact would mean a conditional noexcept on six signatures;
#   that is a live design question recorded in doc/design.md, not something to
#   decide by silencing or by leaving CI red. Suppressed here rather than in
#   the root config, so the check keeps its job over the headers themselves.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -performance-unnecessary-value-param,
  -readability-magic-numbers
